  "world": "\u2b50\u2b50\u2b50 W-UNRESOLVED \u2014 9 OF THE TEN EXCESSES COVER ZERO. Bootstrapping prompts and recomputing the correlation, its matched floor and the overlap TOGETHER on every resample, only 1 of the ten shortfalls have a 95% interval excluding zero. The greedy-oracle cell, the smallest and the one three rounds have reasoned about, has SE 0.0162 against a point excess of +0.0211. \u2b50 The arc has been explaining a quantity its own design cannot resolve, and the honest report for those cells is a bound. \u2b50\u2b50 THE ORDERING GAPS ARE A DIFFERENT MATTER: 0 of 2 exclude zero ({'greedy': 0.0396, 'indep': 0.0511}), so what survives R738 is the ordering and not the individual shortfalls. \u26a0 The interval is conditional on this criterion pool; pricing pool uncertainty would need a second release."
